  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has since secured a $2M budget approved by the executive board. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The project is expanding its team with Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Strategic partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology are being explored and established. The project is moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, with user interface enhancements planned for October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November."
